## Vercel Speed Insights Implementation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js project following the latest official documentation from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart.

### Changes Made

**1. Package Installation**
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` package using npm
- Added package to dependencies in `package.json`
- Updated `package-lock.json` with new dependencies

**2. Code Integration (app/layout.tsx)**
- Added import statement: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next"`
- Added `<SpeedInsights />` component inside the `<body>` tag of the root layout
- Component placed after the `<GlobalProviderWrapper>` to ensure it doesn't interfere with existing application structure

### Implementation Details

The implementation follows the official Vercel documentation for Next.js 13.5+ (App Router):
- Used the framework-specific import path `@vercel/speed-insights/next`
- Placed the component in the root layout file (app/layout.tsx) as recommended
- The SpeedInsights component is now included in every page of the application

### Testing & Verification

✅ **Build Test**: Successfully ran `npm run build` - production build completed without errors
✅ **Linter Test**: Ran ESLint - no new errors introduced by the changes (existing errors are pre-existing and unrelated)
✅ **TypeScript**: Build process included TypeScript compilation which passed successfully

### Next Steps

After deployment to Vercel:
1. Ensure Speed Insights is enabled in the Vercel dashboard for this project
2. The tracking script will automatically be injected at `/_vercel/speed-insights/*`
3. Performance metrics will begin appearing in the Vercel dashboard after users visit the site
4. Metrics typically take a few days to populate with sufficient data

### Files Modified

- `fronted/app/layout.tsx` - Added SpeedInsights component
- `fronted/package.json` - Added @vercel/speed-insights dependency
- `fronted/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies

The implementation is complete and ready for deployment. No additional configuration is required.
